y-difference thresholds defining a cliff.", 'A finding that models are locally smooth across cliffs (ratio ≈ 1) is a negative result about mechanism, but it is precisely the mechanistic explanation for the well-documented AC failure mode and is decision-relevant for trusting these models in lead optimization; we frame either outcome as explaining WHY cliffs are hard at the representational level.', 'All experiments are inference-only on public pretrained models plus small probes/SAEs and public benchmark data (MoleculeACE, ChEMBL), keeping compute at academic scale.']}

