eanest testbed since it explicitly ingests distance-to-hull.", 'Constructing counterfactual contexts requires curated phase diagrams and, ideally, hypothetical competing phases; we use Materials Project phase diagrams and real competing phases where possible, and clearly flag any synthetic competitors.', 'Linear probes recovering a competition direction do not guarantee causal use; we address this with steering and random/formation-energy-direction controls, though distributed encodings may blur single-direction interventions.', 'Some models pool to a single structure embedding, limiting fine-grained analysis; we prioritize models exposing usable per-structure representations and report pooling caveats.', 'A negative result (models encode pointwise formation energy but not the relational competition) is scientifically decisive and directly relevant to trusting hull-conditioned generative discovery pipelines, though it may be perceived as confirmatory of skepticism; we frame either outcome as the first mechanism-defining test of whether crystal FMs represent the convex-hull competition that defines stability.', 'All experiments are inference-only on public pretrained models plus small probes/SAEs and public Materials Project data, keeping compute at academic scale.']}

