mmetry probe: is a recoverable internal chirality direction invariant under 3D rotation yet sign-flipping under mirror reflection, as physics dictates? Second, and most decisively, a mirror-reflection counterfactual: we reflect a molecule's geometry to flip ONLY handedness while exactly preserving all scalar invariants, and test whether the internal chirality signal and the model's enantioselective property prediction flip, whereas an achiral perturbation of matched magnitude does not. Third, causal steering along the pseudoscalar direction should swap enantiomer-dependent predictions. Metrics quantify a pseudoscalar-fidelity index, a mirror-flip-vs-achiral causal asymmetry, and an enantioselective prediction-swap rate. Either outcome sharpens whether molecular foundation models - increasingly used in drug design where the wrong enantiomer can be toxic - represent the handedness mechanism or are blind to it.", 'Experiments': ['1. Models and data: Load pretrained molecular foundation models spanning representation types with usable internal states: 3D atomistic FMs (MACE-MP-0 / atomistic MLIP latents as in Rem3Di, Uni-Mol), and 2D/SMILES chemical FMs (ChemBERTa-2, SMI-TED) that DO ingest stereochemistry tags. Assemble datasets of enantiomer pairs with ground truth: R/S-labeled chiral centers (Chi-Geometry synthetic benchmark for clean isolation, plus real drug-like enantiomer pairs), and enantioselective property data (chiral chromatography elution order, optical rotation / ECD sign, enantiosensitive docking scores or protein-binding affinities). For 3D models, generate paired conformers of a molecule and its exact mirror image. All experiments are inference-only plus small probes.', '2. Baseline decodability: Train linear probes on internal representations (per layer) to decode (a) achiral scalar features (element counts, connectivity, distances) and (b) R/S configuration / handedness. Confirm what is encoded, select best layers, and establish an achiral-substructur